#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199281} :activity/id #uuid "3436fa6e-7d06-5a5e-90bb-b6107d2ecf0e" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048185 :topic/id #uuid "8698dcb0-d732-5f62-8605-520598e45185" :topic/math-academy-id 4145} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199280 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198378 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198020 :question/id #uuid "9a1112c0-db94-5572-ba53-b78116b7c273" :question/math-academy-id "e-12355"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050188} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050508}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198584} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198585} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278446} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278470} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278471} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278507} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398507} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398534} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421783} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434830} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501152} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549979}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"} :step/id #uuid "a6470e60-331b-571e-b3d2-ff5a04e501fb" :step/math-academy-id 44278 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199283}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199281 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199465 :tutorial/content "Recall that the flux of the vector field $\\mathbf F$ across a smooth, orientable surface $S$ with respect to the unit normal vector $\\mathbf{n}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf F \\cdot \\textrm{d} \\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S  \\mathbf F \\cdot {\\color{blue}\\mathbf{n}} \\,\\textrm{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{n}}$ is a unit normal vector that defines the orientation of the surface.\n\n![](images/9a/9aa63a1e4f1d278cef6c53600e8fb9c60829de972ba7409afdc32837ecbc3e07.png)\n\nIf $S$ is given by a parametric equation of the form \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}=\\mathbf{r}(u,v), \\qquad (u,v)\\in D\\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^2,\n$$\n\nwe can determine the unit normal vector using the fundamental product as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{n}} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v}{\\| \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\|}\n$$\n\n \n\nSubstituting this into the formula for the flux, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\frac{{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}}{‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖}\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot \\frac{{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}}{‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖}\\,‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $S$ is a smooth, orientable surface given in parametric form by $\\mathbf{r}=\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^2,$ then the flux of the vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ across $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf F \\cdot \\textrm{d} \\mathbf{S} = \\iint\\limits_D  \\mathbf F(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\: \\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nLet's see some examples." :tutorial/id #uuid "32db1cfe-d870-502c-a709-0a79ee70a616" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7633 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "36b6d02c-b1f4-58b5-b15a-0a072e1d5cac" :step/math-academy-id 44280 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199280}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199283 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198380 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198022 :question/id #uuid "0364a11f-e567-517e-acf2-471708dbdc0a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12358"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531837} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198586} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198592} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278448} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278449} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278450} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278455} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278459} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278461} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421784} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421785} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434831} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531811} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531812} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531818} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531826} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531827}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"} :step/id #uuid "d2e640e5-2cd0-57f1-8576-f38b3f6df4a4" :step/math-academy-id 44283}] :activity/title "Calculating Flux Through Parametric Surfaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186198487}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434834} :activity/id #uuid "67831f4f-8138-536f-9514-23aeb5868445" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048185 :topic/id #uuid "8698dcb0-d732-5f62-8605-520598e45185" :topic/math-academy-id 4145} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434832 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434830 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02b1374a-677b-550b-816a-6cbd02c5f061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434818} {:answer/id #uuid "29ead56c-2949-5fb0-8895-cdd6a87df4b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434820} {:answer/id #uuid "bb3bf5e7-fb1f-5845-863a-15bfb2564e17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434824} {:answer/id #uuid "c3e03b7e-e933-5e07-a534-f79399c89baf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434825} {:answer/id #uuid "c757d8e1-3c0b-5fc9-9360-e929a186b1fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434826}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434820} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1855324-ee18-529c-ba15-53c93565cb17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434829}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "22bda1b7-731c-5be9-8f1b-6668d9e068b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-161253" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,xz,\\,yz⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{u}^{2},\\,v⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}auv+b{u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2u,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2u \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,-1,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\,xz,\\,yz⟩{|}_{x=u\\,y={u}^{2}\\,z=v} \\\\  & =⟨v,\\,uv,\\,{u}^{2}v⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨v,\\,uv,\\,{u}^{2}v⟩\\cdot ⟨2u,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =v\\cdot 2u+uv\\cdot (-1)+{u}^{2}v\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2uv-uv+0 \\\\  & =uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1\\cdot uv+0\\cdot {u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=1+0=1.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "764dfadc-7353-5f72-bb5e-9db6eccbfeca" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434833}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434833 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434831 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c4ed277-51d3-5190-9f15-e73dd884cf47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434819} {:answer/id #uuid "471dabbc-d133-52dc-b559-394801c709a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434821} {:answer/id #uuid "777af6b2-9aef-5099-aac7-98b1ec37120e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434822} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1f231c-84b6-5409-b4c5-4c9196b18b4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434823} {:answer/id #uuid "de47629f-21da-52b1-941b-ae2f3625cecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434827}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434819} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a1a0c12-6b57-5589-b4e1-416cdc457a68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f5815497-10bb-5d31-b1ef-c78b6eb79a17" :question/math-academy-id "q-161259" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,uv⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 0,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-u-v,\\,v-u,\\,2⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-u-v,\\,v-u,\\,2⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨x,\\,y,\\,-z⟩|}_{x=u+v\\,y=v-u\\,z=uv} \\\\  & =⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,-uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,-uv⟩\\cdot ⟨-u-v,\\,v-u,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =(u+v)\\cdot (-u-v)+(v-u)\\cdot (v-u)+(-uv)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-{u}^{2}-2uv-{v}^{2}+{v}^{2}-2uv+{u}^{2}-2uv \\\\  & =-6uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-6uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}uv\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{0}^{1}v\\,\\text{d}v{\\int }_{-2}^{0}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6\\cdot [\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}]_{0}^{1}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9468f911-b5bd-557b-9a6f-8e025c4a65c6"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434834 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198585 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "194750cf-4b33-5153-97c1-bd1b0f21c3c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8u{v}^{3}+8{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275713} {:answer/id #uuid "30772c46-8461-5daa-94aa-ff5b8a754f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8u{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275909} {:answer/id #uuid "45100deb-1ec8-5bbb-b0b4-3c26c5616332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2u{v}^{3}+4{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276086} {:answer/id #uuid "45e6001c-4deb-5a8c-b01f-01531e4489d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4u{v}^{3}+2{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276094} {:answer/id #uuid "936bab95-9822-587d-80ac-54eded632448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276811}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276811} :answer-field/id #uuid "f81d9840-6037-5557-81d1-599235b0ea5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9fcf8673-a62b-588a-8020-ca78007689b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160840" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨2x+y,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨-{u}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2x+y,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩{|}_{x=-{u}^{2}\\,y=2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨2(-{u}^{2})+(2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}),\\,2({v}^{2}),\\,(2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2})+{v}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{v}^{2},\\,2{v}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-{v}^{2},\\,2{v}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩ \\\\  & =(-{v}^{2})\\cdot 8uv+2{v}^{2}\\cdot 4uv+2{u}^{2}\\cdot 4uv \\\\  & =-8u{v}^{3}+8u{v}^{3}+8{u}^{3}v \\\\  & =8{u}^{3}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,8{u}^{3}v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e88e2f68-fd58-50c1-9108-060ce4b3171a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434832}}] :activity/title "Calculating Flux Through Parametric Surfaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434817}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550085} :activity/id #uuid "d772e5b9-52ff-5f18-8921-39a21fd1c86c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048185 :topic/id #uuid "8698dcb0-d732-5f62-8605-520598e45185" :topic/math-academy-id 4145} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550085 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421784 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a219dca-1e12-574f-9fc3-d709a89775ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421769} {:answer/id #uuid "4b502ee2-042d-5a3e-86ae-ba6ad14e00b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421770} {:answer/id #uuid "5be10e6b-2fc0-5157-8d4c-a6365644fb4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421771} {:answer/id #uuid "ac272ec2-a123-566b-9ae4-94a591001c16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421776} {:answer/id #uuid "bb4a967e-d128-5262-a38b-86976eb912e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{22}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421777}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421770} :answer-field/id #uuid "de26f158-7713-5413-99c7-ec6ea96881bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4c963e37-fb2b-5cec-bc6e-5cbde0fb10aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-161258" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3x,\\,-{y}^{2},\\,2⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨3uv,\\,u,\\,-v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-1,\\,3v,\\,-3u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-1,\\,3v,\\,-3u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨3x,\\,-{y}^{2},\\,2⟩|}_{x=3uv\\,y=u\\,z=-v} \\\\  & =⟨3(3uv),\\,-{u}^{2},\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9uv,\\,-{u}^{2},\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨9uv,\\,-{u}^{2},\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,3v,\\,-3u⟩ \\\\  & =9uv\\cdot (-1)+(-{u}^{2})\\cdot 3v+2\\cdot (-3u) \\\\  & =-9uv-3{u}^{2}v-6u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3x,\\,-{y}^{2},\\,2⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-9uv-3{u}^{2}v-6u)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-9uv-3{u}^{2}v-6u)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-\\frac{9}{2}{u}^{2}v-{u}^{3}v-3{u}^{2}]}_{u=0}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{11}{2}v-3)\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{11}{4}{v}^{2}-3v]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{4}-3 \\\\  & =-\\frac{23}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ac2ffa16-958c-5789-909d-6652b7b2609d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550094}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550094 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278448 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4eb1ebbc-1b66-59c6-bc4c-36473d96ba4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276175} {:answer/id #uuid "85d8c729-3067-5308-8ef9-00bf4d3de7e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276678} {:answer/id #uuid "89edd3d9-c58a-5b81-ba4b-f7481df906e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276723} {:answer/id #uuid "a74d2bae-d261-5258-af7b-a10ec79ffeaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276985} {:answer/id #uuid "dc49e905-67e7-5a8f-9ad4-5d61bb70fa97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277407}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276175} :answer-field/id #uuid "8068e66d-fe19-5730-b61d-8b3c05169a3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277949}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "24885575-8fa2-5424-9a08-3593cc23273c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161260" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨y+z,\\,x+z,\\,1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u-v,\\,2,\\,{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨0,\\,-2v,\\,0⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨0,\\,-2v,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨y+z,\\,x+z,\\,1⟩|}_{x=u-v\\,y=2\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨2+{v}^{2},\\,u-v+{v}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨2+{v}^{2},\\,u-v+{v}^{2},\\,1⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,-2v,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =(2+{v}^{2})\\cdot 0+(u-v+{v}^{2})\\cdot (-2v)+1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-2uv+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨y+z,\\,x+z,\\,1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-2uv+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2uv+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3})\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[-{u}^{2}v+2u{v}^{2}-2u{v}^{3}]_{u=0}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-v+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3})\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b5fed080-f431-544b-ac5b-4f64ca581a1a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550119}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550111 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278471 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bd609ae-e864-57b8-94a4-273742d368ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275735} {:answer/id #uuid "2ccb8e67-96de-5752-b3c3-d11e0af4993a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275881} {:answer/id #uuid "54d35ae5-86bd-5395-8972-05d0d8d00e47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276231} {:answer/id #uuid "af78fb93-58e2-566e-a85b-fc76c0f645fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277047} {:answer/id #uuid "f88b3e2e-dffa-5fc2-9b42-e62568668267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277651}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276231} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8a58223-7188-508a-9949-c05e00640b00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8ba2bc0a-f01f-56b1-8fa8-5c3da0d50d17" :question/math-academy-id "q-161306" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨x-\\frac{1}{z},\\,y+\\frac{1}{z},\\,z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u{e}^{v},\\,u{e}^{-v},\\,u⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}a{e}^{v}+b{e}^{-v}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{e}^{v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{e}^{-v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{v},\\,{e}^{-v},\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u{e}^{v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u{e}^{-v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u{e}^{v},\\,-u{e}^{-v},\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ {e}^{v} & {e}^{-v} & 1 \\\\ u{e}^{v} & -u{e}^{-v} & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-v} & 1 \\\\ -u{e}^{-v} & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{v} & 1 \\\\ u{e}^{v} & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{v} & {e}^{-v} \\\\ u{e}^{v} & -u{e}^{-v}\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u{e}^{-v},\\,u{e}^{v},\\,-2u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x-\\frac{1}{z},\\,y+\\frac{1}{z},\\,z⟩{|}_{x=u{e}^{v}\\,y=u{e}^{-v}\\,z=u} \\\\  & =⟨u{e}^{v}-\\frac{1}{u},\\,u{e}^{-v}+\\frac{1}{u},\\,u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u{e}^{v}-\\frac{1}{u},\\,u{e}^{-v}+\\frac{1}{u},\\,u⟩\\cdot ⟨u{e}^{-v},\\,u{e}^{v},\\,-2u⟩ \\\\  & =(u{e}^{v}-\\frac{1}{u})\\cdot u{e}^{-v}+(u{e}^{-v}+\\frac{1}{u})\\cdot u{e}^{v}+u\\cdot (-2u) \\\\  & ={u}^{2}-{e}^{-v}+{u}^{2}+{e}^{v}-2{u}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{v}-{e}^{-v}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1\\cdot {e}^{v}+(-1)\\cdot {e}^{-v}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=1-1=0.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e0c69e8f-7604-5834-a785-1955ecbd11bc"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550113 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549979 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67d2eb68-0652-5e48-b001-a45c2700c7e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549515} {:answer/id #uuid "94798f5c-574c-53cd-bb0e-eb9396410fae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549605} {:answer/id #uuid "c199e1eb-7983-554d-81aa-b675e5252dbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549680} {:answer/id #uuid "e8394076-ef1d-5d29-b139-67414f969f56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549743} {:answer/id #uuid "ee167035-8819-5d49-80a8-31c9bebffaab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549753}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549515} :answer-field/id #uuid "63772144-9630-582a-8d79-f08320bc64ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8e8e30b7-68c9-50ac-bfbf-42853c6a4c1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-161305" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,xz⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{v}^{2},\\,uv⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}a{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+bu{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & v \\\\ 0 & 2v & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & v \\\\ 2v & u\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & v \\\\ 0 & u\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-u,\\,2v⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x,\\,y,\\,xz⟩{|}_{x=u\\,y={v}^{2}\\,z=uv} \\\\  & =⟨u,\\,{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}v⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u,\\,{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-u,\\,2v⟩ \\\\  & =u\\cdot (-2{v}^{2})+{v}^{2}\\cdot (-u)+{u}^{2}v\\cdot 2v \\\\  & =-2u{v}^{2}-u{v}^{2}+2{u}^{2}{v}^{2} \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}-3u{v}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2\\cdot {u}^{2}{v}^{2}+(-3)\\cdot u{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=2-3=-1.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ef98d794-5919-5339-9e62-26bb3d70695c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550111}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550119 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278455 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4087a83f-b6d4-59eb-ad43-5778e62db807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276039} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf11252-5492-5171-bafa-fea2eb4849ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276157} {:answer/id #uuid "9a0daa63-b87d-58b0-ad93-81d0749be7b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276857} {:answer/id #uuid "bb812a7c-457e-5b53-bb9a-157b69c0ee22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277146} {:answer/id #uuid "dc487f46-d4f7-596b-b4d5-ade4f4727666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277406}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276157} :answer-field/id #uuid "09628fb2-5798-5e67-a99b-89a6c4a88382" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277743}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "75e371a5-e04a-5fb9-938c-f538e06e2f93" :question/math-academy-id "q-161273" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,0,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u-v,\\,v-u,\\,-2uv⟩\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-2uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-2v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-2uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-2u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & -2v \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2v \\\\ 1 & -2u\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2v \\\\ -1 & -2u\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u+2v,\\,2u+2v,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨x,\\,0,\\,y⟩|}_{x=u-v\\,y=v-u\\,z=-2uv} \\\\  & =⟨u-v,\\,0,\\,v-u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u-v,\\,0,\\,v-u⟩\\cdot ⟨2u+2v,\\,2u+2v,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =(u-v)\\cdot (2u+2v)+0\\cdot (2u+2v)+(v-u)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,0,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}-u{v}^{2}]}_{u=0}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{1}{3}-{v}^{2})\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{[\\frac{1}{3}v-\\frac{1}{3}{v}^{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "fe42edc3-5c6d-5e3c-87fb-a75dfa963a99" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550113}}] :activity/title "Calculating Flux Through Parametric Surfaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549316}]}
